  "notes": "FORMAL VOCABULARY:\n{関与|かんよ} is a formal term often used in news, legal, and official contexts.\n\nUSAGE:\n- In neutral contexts, it means general involvement or participation.\n- In negative contexts, it implies being implicated in wrongdoing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {関与|かんよ}する - to be involved in\n- {関与|かんよ}を{認|みと}める - to admit involvement\n- {関与|かんよ}を{否定|ひてい}する - to deny involvement\n- {直接|ちょくせつ}{関与|かんよ} - direct involvement\n- {間接|かんせつ}{関与|かんよ} - indirect involvement\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {参加|さんか} - participation (more positive)\n- {関係|かんけい} - relation, connection (broader)\n- {介入|かいにゅう} - intervention",
